save__mmfdb_artifact.is_sidecar
   _item.name                "_mmfdb_artifact.is_sidecar"
   _item.category_id         mmfdb_artifact
   _item_type.code           int
   _item.mandatory_code      no
   _mmfdb_schema.table_name  mmfdb_artifact
   _mmfdb_schema.column_name is_sidecar
   _item_description.description
;     Whether this artifact is a file that only exists BESIDE another one and
;     cannot be read alone.
;
;     A Becker & Hickl `.spc` keeps half its header in a `.set` next to it: hand
;     a reader the `.spc` on its own and it decodes with the wrong resolution
;     and no error. The `.set` is therefore not a second measurement and not a
;     derived result -- the two categories a container otherwise has -- and
;     listing it as either misleads. It is a part of its primary, and the
;     primary is named by _mmfdb_edge.source_node_id on the sidecar.
;
;     A reader extracting the measurement must extract the sidecars with it; a
;     reader enumerating what a container holds should not count them as
;     measurements. 1 for a sidecar, 0 or absent otherwise.
;
    loop_
    _item_enumeration.value
    _item_enumeration.detail
      0  "a file that stands on its own"
      1  "a sidecar; unreadable without the artifact it accompanies"

