save__mmfdb_operation.dictionary_version
   _item.name                "_mmfdb_operation.dictionary_version"
   _item.category_id         mmfdb_operation
   _item_type.code           code
   _item.mandatory_code      no
   _mmfdb_schema.table_name  mmfdb_operation
   _mmfdb_schema.column_name dictionary_version
   _item_description.description
;     The ``_dictionary.version`` of mmfdb_flr_ext.dic in force when this
;     operation was recorded.  An operation is tagged with controlled terms,
;     and a term can be renamed or withdrawn by a later revision; without this
;     the row cannot say which vocabulary it meant, and a reader has no way to
;     tell drift from a typo.
;

save__mmfdb_operation.dictionary_hash
   _item.name                "_mmfdb_operation.dictionary_hash"
   _item.category_id         mmfdb_operation
   _item_type.code           code
   _item.mandatory_code      no
   _mmfdb_schema.table_name  mmfdb_operation
   _mmfdb_schema.column_name dictionary_hash
   _item_description.description
;     SHA-256 of the bytes of mmfdb_flr_ext.dic in force when this operation
;     was recorded, lowercase hexadecimal.  A version is what an author
;     declares; this is what was actually loaded, and the two disagree exactly
;     when someone edited a dictionary without bumping it.
;

